WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.910
In the new movie "The Batman," Bruce Wayne
quickly meets and partners up with Selina

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.779
Kyle, also known to DC fans as Catwoman.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:12.660
The two have an intensely intertwined story,
with Bruce helping Selina uncover the fate

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.779
of her roommate and the truth about her father,
Carmine Falcone.

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:20.999
But there's one other important figure in
Selina's life who plays a key role in the

00:00:20.999 --> 00:00:23.909
film's story — and she never even shows
up on screen.

00:00:23.909 --> 00:00:26.169
This is her mother, Maria Kyle.

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:30.199
Selina explains her backstory to Bruce one
night, telling him about how her mother worked

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:33.040
at the Iceberg Lounge and met Falcone there.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.520
Of course, then this romance led to her, and
she spends most of her early childhood years

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.180
just hanging out at the establishment.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.690
As she talks about her history, it becomes
clear that a lot of what she does is based

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.580
around this past experience.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:49.280
While she might claim to want to get away
from Gotham, Selina can't seem to leave her

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.780
connection to Falcone and what happened to
her mother behind.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.960
It's obvious that Selina loves her mother
very dearly, leading her to take her father's

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.520
abandonment more personally.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.970
Then, when her roommate ends up dead in a
similar fashion as her mother, Selina's drive

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.220
for answers grows even stronger.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.470
But casual fans of the DCEU tuning in to watch
"The Batman" might not know a lot about Selina's

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.810
backstory, and there's a lot about her mother,
Maria, that the movie doesn't go into.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.670
In "The Batman," viewers only really know
anything about Maria based on what Selina

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:20.890
describes to Bruce or Falcone.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.120
But with all the information the movie provides,
it appears that this version of Maria is a

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.800
loving mother who is just unlucky in life.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.310
Maria works at the Iceberg Lounge both before
and after giving birth to Selina, but unfortunately,

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.810
she is murdered when Selina is very young,
and for a long time, Selina doesn't know who

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:38.970
is responsible.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:43.610
Without a real direction in life, Selina grows
up and develops the thieving skills she exhibits

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:48.260
in the movie, intending to steal some cash,
leave Gotham, and start over.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:52.670
Aside from her career and relationship with
Falcone, "The Batman" doesn't reveal too much

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.740
else about Selina's mother.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.920
But one thing is crystal clear, and that's
the fact that Selina clearly loves her mother

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.430
very much and holds no resentment or bad feelings
over how she grows up.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:08.340
Instead, all of her grief, hate, and loneliness
is targeted at Falcone, who she knows is her

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.150
father but who has zero involvement in her
life, leaving her to grow up all alone after

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.150
Maria's death.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.640
In the comics, Selina's relationship with
her mother is a little more complicated, and

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.800
if you can believe it, a little more traumatic
too.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.920
As revealed in the solo series, "Catwoman,"
Volume 2, which ran from 1993 to 2001, when

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.530
Selina was a child, her mother Maria was in
an abusive marriage with Selina's father,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.530
Brian Kyle.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:37.310
At one point, Brian says that Maria's family
are refugees, possibly from Cuba, and she

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:41.790
likely speaks both English and Spanish, something
Brian berates her for.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.170
Along with that, Maria suffers from mental
illness and faces money pressures to support

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:50.700
the family, which includes a younger sister
Selina doesn't have in the film named Maggie

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.700
Kyle.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.180
Unfortunately, Maria dies by suicide when
Selina is very young, and she is the one to

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.230
discover her.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:02.060
In the aftermath of her mother's death, Selina's
father turns to drinking and she is eventually

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:07.069
separated from her sister, leading to her
growing up on the street and taking up thievery.

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:11.700
Luckily, Selina holds on to one connection
to her mother in the form of gymnastics, which

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.740
her mother enrolls her in before her death.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:18.280
Selina exhibits a natural skill for gymnastics
and it clearly helps her later on once she

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.590
becomes Catwoman.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:25.250
In the comics, there's also a rumor that Carmine
Falcone and his wife Louisa Falcone are Selina's

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.380
real parents, though it's never confirmed,
and of course, the film makes it clear that

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.550
Falcone is at least her father.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.000
Relating to that, the comics don't show if
or how Maria and Falcone could've crossed

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.849
paths, although their connection is a major
focus of Selina's story in "The Batman."

